cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "circuitpharm: receptor-resolved pharmacology coupled to spiking neural circuits, with enforced reliability tiers"
abstract: >-
  A multiscale instrument that takes a compound's measured receptor activity and propagates
  it to circuit-level and motor/autonomic endpoints (respiratory rhythm, spinal stretch
  reflex, closed-loop locomotion), attaching an explicit reliability tier to every quantity
  it reports. Reading a quantity marked VOID raises rather than returning a caveated
  number. The package declines to close two links in the chain from chemical structure to
  behaviour: allosteric efficacy is taken as a measured input rather than predicted from
  structure, and behaviour is restricted to outputs whose generating circuits are
  biophysically modellable. Catalogued modelling failure modes are shipped as executable
  regression tests.
type: software
